@model MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages.Settings.ProductCategories.IndexModel
@* =====================================================================
   Settings/ProductCategories/_ListState.cshtml — NEW (073).

   The search, the filters and the page, as hidden fields. Dropped into
   every POST form on the page:

       <partial name="_ListState" model="Model" />

   WHY EVERY FORM NEEDS IT

   Each handler ends with RedirectToPage(ReturnRoute()), and ReturnRoute
   is built from the page model's bound properties. On a POST those
   properties bind from the FORM, not from the URL the user is looking
   at — so without these fields every save, toggle, remove and reorder
   would redirect to page 1 of an unfiltered list.

   The symptom is mild and maddening: switch three categories off in a
   row, and after each one you are back at the top of the list hunting
   for where you were.

   They bind on a POST because the properties are
   [BindProperty(SupportsGet = true)] — SupportsGet ADDS GET binding, it
   does not remove the POST binding every [BindProperty] has.
   ===================================================================== *@

<input type="hidden" name="q" value="@Model.SearchTerm" />
<input type="hidden" name="status" value="@Model.StatusFilter" />
<input type="hidden" name="kind" value="@Model.KindFilter" />
<input type="hidden" name="PageNumber" value="@Model.PageNumber" />
<input type="hidden" name="PageSize" value="@Model.PageSize" />
